{"corrections":["Agent-authored preserved parent provenance for this continuing objective; this is not a new user utterance. Original immutable context SHA256 9e234588b44a3310e115541df26b8c2765e20dc40c4a8224cb471d4f3756ed14 follows exactly:\n{\"corrections\":[\"and once you done - monitor PRs until completion, stop only when ALL of them are merged successfully with dev\",\"fix any issues on the way\",\"PR in self_host is considered relevant only if it affects github agents functionality\",\"check RPI agents, their, especially those who waiting for user approval\",\"also update rpi agents to ALWAYS use recommended options when they have questions about plan/feature implementation/correction\",\"and I want to get messages only about user approvals / tg requested feature implemntation status / pr mergres with dev / released / merges with main\",\"also restart agents who are waiting user's approval so that use this new policy\",\"also for tg questions, allow respond in github as well\",\"ok, fix those tooling issues\",\"one asks me to provide agents.md WTF, looks like a tooling issue as well\",\"also I've noticed that user answers to agent's question recorded and posted in PR, but agent's question is not visible => not enough context, fix that as well, record both questions and answers\",\"answer to agents in PRs\",\"also raise RPI agents concurrency to 10\",\"do not forget \\\"agent:writing\\\" labels\",\"provide reliable fix so that does not occur again\",\"for \\\"ALWAYS use reccomended\\\" let's just spawn \\\"plan resolver\\\" agent on RPI which checks that recommended options and if they are aligned with user request -approves them. Also add \\\"orchestrator\\\" agent which is spawned every 30 minutes (no more than 1 such agent) IF at least 1 PR is open and  it basically does what you do now: finds issues in rpi agents toolkit, fixes them, etc. still no heavy checks on rpi. but it may edit atk and self host dirs. If nothng to fix - that agent ceases to exist\",\"if it is not addressing it - fix it so it does that\",\"is orchestrator fixing #9?\",\"picker_diagnostic_replan: Diagnostics first (Recommended)\\nReason: The full recorded request authorizes reliable repairs along the way and requires monitoring through every qualifying PR's successful dev merge. The current author replan reports that assigned composed cells, SVGs and native-size PNG retain the heading, while historical comparison evidence does not establish the cause of the reported character loss. Those are supplied diagnostic statements, not this reviewer's independent visual finding or proof of a failing layer. Obtaining bounded, head/dev-bound GitHub glyph/rasterization/scaling diagnostics before cause-specific planning is therefore consistent with the existing Repair text fidelity choice: trace the first demonstrated divergence and repair only the responsible layer. It does not cancel the text-fidelity objective or supersede the settled Stable geometry and assertions repair. Preserve unpublished CI repairs and existing PR39 behavior; obtain fresh planning and independent plan review after evidence acquisition. The coordinator owns retrieving this evidence; no owner preference, credential, upload or new authorization is necessary for this strategy choice. All final-head checks and complete fresh visual/source review remain required. Preserve the full parent objective: PR39 remains PR37's separate visual-repair dependency; retain all SQL Explorer repairs, exact heading, completion placement/non-overlap/containment, journal failure and recovery behavior, regressions, quality and coverage baselines, scene IDs/stress cases, all 46 full-scene geometry and individual PNG gates, independent plan/source review and final-head fast CI. Preserve exporter/producer-consumer/activation and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry dependencies; do not treat historical captures, unpublished edits or completed deployments as new success or rerun a completed rollout. Continue all qualifying PRs and resulting repairs to successful dev merges. Retain concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, full questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent resolver alignment, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance, and notification limits. Preserve genuine credentials/provenance/security, owner veto/cancel and protected exact-head holds. This transparent automated independent strategy assessment is not an owner answer, visual pass, plan/code/protected approval, deployment instruction or completion claim. Execute no candidate programs/tests/renders on the Pi; diagnostics and validation run through isolated GitHub mechanisms.\",\"I allow you to approve instead of me\"],\"decisions\":[{\"choice\":\"journal_error_status: Existing error message (Recommended)\\nReason: The reader already returns page.warning on failure and an empty warning for successful zero-result reads. The assigned journal-error PNG confirms the misleading combined status. Showing the warning alone fixes this demonstrated issue under the request to fix issues along the way. Focused failure/recovery coverage, fresh complete GitHub visual review and exact-head validation remain required. PR #39 and the complete parent objective remain intact, including monitoring and repairs until all relevant PRs merge successfully into dev, notification limits, lifecycle labels and owner authority gates. No Pi execution or protected approval is authorized.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should this repair distinguish journal read failures from successful searches with zero results, while preserving PR #39 and the complete parent objective?\\nExisting error message (Recommended): Show page.warning alone on failure; retain the empty-result message for successful zero-result reads. Add focused failure/recovery coverage and require fresh complete GitHub visual review and exact-head validation.\\nExplicit failure field: Add a defaulted failure indicator to JournalPage, update its reader and UI consumers, and test compatibility alongside the same visual and GitHub validation gates.\"]},{\"choice\":\"completion_placement: Anchor below row (Recommended)\\nReason: The pinned completion PNGs show menus overlapping the active SQL row, and source positions them using an offset without full parent-coordinate conversion. Accounting for the rendered caret row, ruler and scrolling, with above-row fallback, addresses this demonstrated issue under 'fix any issues on the way' and the reliable-fix requirement. Focused geometry/interaction regressions and fresh complete GitHub visual review remain required, alongside final-head validation and independent review. This leaf repair preserves PR #39 and the complete parent objective: all relevant PRs and resulting repairs must merge successfully into dev; retain notification limits, lifecycle labels, recorded question/answer context, concurrency and orchestrator requirements, dependency gates and owner authority. No Pi execution, protected exact-head approval, or plan/code approval is granted.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should the repair position SQL completion menus while preserving PR #39 and the complete parent objective?\\nAnchor below row (Recommended): Use the rendered caret row in the menu parent’s coordinates, accounting for the ruler and scrolling; keep the active row unobscured, fit above when needed, and add focused geometry and interaction regressions plus fresh full GitHub visual review.\"]},{\"choice\":\"ci_repair_approach: Stable geometry and assertions (Recommended)\\nReason: The request authorizes fixing issues along the way and requires a reliable repair. Stable parent-relative placement and settled sizing address the popup positioning logic while retaining containment and active-row non-overlap guarantees. Recorded CI evidence supports comparing journal display text compatibly; this must preserve exact expected text and failure/recovery behavior. Fixing lint/type findings without weakening gates preserves required validation. Fresh complete GitHub visual review, focused regressions, independent plan and implementation reviews, and final-head CI remain mandatory; assigned evidence validates neither unpublished edits nor a future head. Preserve PR #39’s existing changes and dependencies and continue the complete parent monitoring/repair objective until all relevant PRs merge successfully into dev. Retain notification limits, concurrency 10, agent:writing labels, complete question/answer records, authenticated GitHub/Telegram responses, resolver and orchestrator requirements, and the GitHub-agent-only relevance restriction for self_host. No local/Pi execution, credentials decision, owner veto/cancel decision, protected exact-head approval, or plan/code approval is granted.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should PR #39’s current-head CI failures be repaired while preserving its existing changes and the complete parent objective?\\nStable geometry and assertions (Recommended): Use a stable parent-relative popup origin and settled layout sizing; preserve containment/non-overlap guards, compare journal display text compatibly, and fix new lint/type findings without weakening gates. Require focused regressions, full fresh GitHub visual review, independent reviews and final-head CI; retain all parent monitoring and authority requirements.\"]},{\"choice\":\"picker_text_repair: Repair text fidelity (Recommended)\\nReason: The request authorizes fixing issues along the way and requires reliable prevention. Source picker.py contains the correct '.connections' heading, while the assigned full database-picker PNG for published head 6aefc2eff5e37b6d3e98a819ed00b40c9fb244d7 visibly loses its c. Tracing and repairing the responsible application/export layer with a focused regression addresses the demonstrated defect without inventing its cause. Fresh complete GitHub visual review, independent plan/source review and final-head CI remain required; existing evidence validates neither unpublished changes nor a future head. Preserve PR #39's existing changes, settled CI repair, dependencies and the root monitoring/repair objective until all relevant PRs merge successfully into dev, including notification limits, concurrency 10, agent:writing labels, complete question/answer records, authenticated GitHub/Telegram responses, resolver/orchestrator requirements and the GitHub-agent-only self_host restriction. No local/Pi execution, credentials decision, owner veto/cancellation decision, protected exact-head approval or plan/code approval is granted.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should PR #39 address the verified database-picker heading defect while preserving the settled CI repair and complete parent objective?\\nRepair text fidelity (Recommended): Locate where the correct .connections text loses its c, fix the responsible application/export layer, add a focused regression, and require fresh complete GitHub visual review plus independent plan/source review and final-head CI. Preserve existing PR changes, all parent monitoring/dependency requirements and owner authority gates.\"]},{\"choice\":\"picker_evidence_outcome: Evidence-based closure (Recommended)\\nReason: The request authorizes reliable repairs of demonstrated issues, not speculative rendering changes. The assigned published-head picker PNG and receipt do not establish character loss. Appending a factual correction preserves complete question/answer history. Closure remains conditional on fresh complete 46-scene GitHub geometry and full-PNG review, with unresolved acceptance uncertainty requiring bounded coordinator-owned diagnostics and demonstrated defects requiring cause-specific replanning and independent review. Preserve the exact heading, existing SQL Explorer repairs, unpublished CI repairs, regressions, quality/coverage gates, independent plan/full-feature/source reviews and exact final-head CI. Retain PR39/PR37 and all exporter, producer-consumer, activation and PR10/PR9 ancestry dependencies; continue monitoring and repairs until every qualifying PR merges successfully into dev. All concurrency, lifecycle-label, authenticated-reply, resolver/orchestrator, notification and self_host relevance requirements remain binding. No Pi execution, owner answer, protected approval, plan/code approval or completion claim is granted.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should the revised plan handle the corrected picker evidence when no text-fidelity defect is demonstrated, while preserving PR #39’s settled repairs and complete parent objective?\\nEvidence-based closure (Recommended): Append the factual correction without rewriting question/answer history; preserve the exact heading, useful coverage and unpublished CI repairs. Require fresh complete 46-scene GitHub geometry/full-PNG review. If the heading passes, close this allegation without a speculative rendering change or mandatory defect regression. If a specific acceptance uncertainty remains, the coordinator obtains bounded candidate/base/task/run-bound diagnostics; inconclusive evidence remains unresolved. A demonstrated defect requires cause-specific replanning and independent review. Retain independent full-feature/source review, exact final-head CI, all parent monitoring/dependency requirements and genuine owner/security/protected holds.\"]},{\"choice\":\"fragment_repair_path: Bounded correction (Recommended)\\nReason: The owned fragment lacks the '- ' prefix required by the immutable dev-base fragment contract. Correcting that format is supported by the request to fix issues reliably. Coordinator retrieval of complete exact-head failed-job logs before cause-specific CI replanning avoids inventing failure causes. This choice retains existing PR changes, independent reviews, all 46 full-scene geometry and individual PNG gates, final-head CI, dependencies, and monitoring until every qualifying PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev. All notification, lifecycle, concurrency, resolver/orchestrator, authenticated-history and owner-authority requirements remain binding. No local/Pi execution, owner answer, plan/code approval or protected exact-head approval is granted.\",\"questions\":[\"1. Should this correction repair the verified fragment format while retaining the complete parent objective and requiring coordinator-owned diagnosis of the current-head CI failures?\\nBounded correction (Recommended): Replace the owned fragment with one concise '- ' bullet; preserve all PR changes and gates. Have the coordinator fetch complete exact-head failed-job logs before cause-specific CI replanning and independent review; retain full visual/source validation and monitoring through all qualifying dev merges.\"]},{\"choice\":\"pr39_ci_diagnostic_strategy: Bounded GitHub diagnostics (Recommended)\\nReason: The recorded request authorizes reliable repairs along the way, and its authenticated diagnostics-first correction supports coordinator-owned isolated GitHub evidence before cause-specific planning. Candidate/dev/task/run-bound geometry and removal-lifecycle diagnostics across both supported Textual lines address the stated uncertainty without guessing causes or requiring owner-supplied evidence. Readiness, viewport-edge and lint repairs remain contingent on verified evidence and fresh independent plan review; this assessment does not establish those causes. Preserve incoming dev coordinator code/tests/docs, existing and unpublished PR39 repairs, warning-only journal failure/recovery behavior, exact picker heading, completion containment/non-overlap, regressions, quality/coverage baselines, all 46 full-scene geometry and individual PNG gates, independent full-feature/source review and exact-final-head CI. Retain PR39/PR37, exporter/producer-consumer/activation and PR10/PR9 merge/ancestry dependencies. Continue monitoring and repairs until every qualifying PR merges successfully into dev. Retain concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, complete questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent resolver assessment, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance and notification limits. No local/Pi execution is authorized. Genuine owner input, credentials, provenance/security, veto/cancel and protected exact-head holds remain intact. This approves only the recommended strategy's alignment, not a plan, code, protected action, deployment or completion claim.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should planning resolve PR #39’s remaining resize/lifecycle CI uncertainty while preserving its settled repairs and complete parent objective?\\nBounded GitHub diagnostics (Recommended): Have the coordinator obtain candidate/dev/task/run-bound geometry and removal-lifecycle diagnostics through isolated GitHub validation for both supported Textual lines. Preserve incoming dev coordinator code/tests/docs, existing PR changes, warning-only journal status, viewport containment/non-overlap, all 46 visual gates and all parent monitoring/authority requirements. Use the evidence to finish cause-specific planning and independent plan review; repair verified readiness, viewport-edge and lint test issues without weakening assertions. No Pi execution or owner-provided evidence.\"]},{\"choice\":\"pr39_diagnostic_execution_path: Candidate-push diagnostics (Recommended)\\nReason: The full retained owner request requires reliable repairs, no heavy checks onPi, and monitoring until every qualifying PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev. The existing independently resolved diagnostics-first strategy requires candidate/base/task-bound GitHub evidence across both supported Textual lines before selecting causes. The current operational handoff identifies a real execution-path gap: the ordinary test workflow currently persists checkout credentials and has no diagnostic dispatch inputs, while the protected visual workflow only captures Python3.11 scenes. Selecting a bounded ordinary-tests-workflow opt-in diagnostic path on existing agent-visual/<sha> pushes, with checkout credential persistence disabled, concretizes that already selected strategy without inventing dispatch inputs or changing protected controller/dispatch/visual workflows. Python3.11/Textual0.73 andPython3.13/Textual0.89 diagnostic jobs supplement, rather than replace or relax, normal required CI. Ordered instrumentation, full Ruff output and always-retained failures/log/provenance artifacts address the evidence gap even when assertions fail, while preserving strict assertions, complete original failure results and meaningful regression/coverage gates. Independent review of the complete renewed plan is required before instrumentation; resulting exact-bound GitHub evidence then informs separate cause-specific planning and review. This is an implementation-sequence choice within existing repair authorization, not a request for a new owner fact, credentials, protected approval or hold release.\\n\\nTransparent automated coordinator response after separate independent full-task assessment under the owner's standing recommended-options policy. This selects the diagnostic execution strategy only. The renewed complete plan must explicitly limit candidate execution to isolated GitHub runners with read-only permissions and no persisted/write credentials, secrets or privileged controller context available to candidate code; persist-credentials:false is required and is not by itself a complete credential-isolation claim. Limit workflow changes to the ordinary tests workflow; preserve protected controller, dispatch, capture/visual and publishing workflows and genuine exact-head authority boundaries. Use only the actual existing temporary-candidate publication mechanism with exact SHA checks and narrowly activated diagnostics; do not invent unsupported dispatch inputs or infer new publishing rights.\\n\\nKeep ordinary CI triggers, required matrix, assertions, exit status/aggregate failure reporting, coverage/debt floors and strictness intact. The extra diagnostic matrix must retain ordered records, each scenario's original inputs/failure/traceback, framework source+installed version provenance, complete stdout/stderr and Ruff findings even when assertions stop a scenario, and an always-retained bounded artifact index. If a controlled diagnostic runner continues other cases to collect evidence, it must still record and propagate all original failures; no continue-on-error success, hidden truncation, missing-entry-as-pass, forced scene state, relaxed assertion or substituted expected number. Bind source PR/head, preserved checkpoint/patch, actual merged candidate, devbase, full task/plan digest, workflow/run/job/attempt, dependencies, ordered files/lengths/hashes and incompleteness metadata. Any size/collection failure remains explicit unresolved evidence. Separate independent plan review precedes instrumentation; fresh GitHub evidence and separate cause-specific plan review precede behavioral repairs.\\n\\nRetain all existing/unpublished SQLExplorer repairs, incoming current-dev coordinator code/tests/docs and safeguards, completion stable parent-relative geometry/settled sizing/containment/non-overlap/scroll-resize-narrowing/lifecycle/stale-callback/insert-dismiss behavior, warning-only journal failure and recovery, exact picker heading with additive factual corrections and evidence-based no-proven-glyph-defect exit, useful text-fidelity coverage and genuine negative controls. Preserve currentdevf66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01, complete checkpoint/history, owned changelog/docs, strict quality/type/coverage/artifact/compatibility/fastchecks, independent full-feature/source review and all46 scenes at208x47 with every geometry assertion and individual full1280x800 PNG verdict before correction publication. Diagnostic evidence is not feature acceptance.\\n\\nPreserve PR39 as PR37's separate visual-repair dependency, PR37 process-output/history obligations, exporter/producer-consumer/activation gates and PR10 actualPR9 merge/ancestry requirement. Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until every qualifyingPR/resulting repair merges successfully into dev with required validation. Retain concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels includingagent:writing, completeQ/options/A, authenticatedGitHub/Telegram responses, full-task independentresolver/recovery, one30minute/open-PR orchestrator withidleexit, GitHub-agent-onlyself_host relevance and owner notificationlimits. Genuine credentials/authentication/provenance/security, owner-veto/cancel, protected exact-head and actual operational freeze/drain holds remain binding. This authorizes no state/quiescence override, cancelled-rollout retry, frozen-source change or deployment; preserve completed operations and do not rerun them. No candidate programs/tests/scenes/installs run locally or onPi. This is not a newowner preference, plan/source/visual/CI/protected/deployment approval, merge clearance or parentcompletion claim.\\n\\nExact question and all options:\\n1. How should PR #39 obtain credential-free matrix diagnostics while preserving the complete task, existing repairs, validation gates and authority holds?\\nCandidate-push diagnostics (Recommended): Extend only the ordinary tests workflow to recognize existing agent-visual/<sha> pushes and run opt-in diagnostics on Python 3.11/Textual 0.73 and Python 3.13/Textual 0.89. Disable persisted checkout credentials; retain normal CI unchanged in coverage and strictness. Add ordered test instrumentation, always-retained failure/log/provenance artifacts and complete Ruff output bound to candidate/base/task/run/job/attempt/hashes. Keep protected controller/dispatch/visual workflows unchanged. Require independent plan review before instrumentation, then GitHub evidence and separately reviewed cause-specific repair planning.\\n\\nIndependent resolution SHA256 65f808e8dfa977102b74232c9ec674639d386a241447ea8ecbdbd4f9e65a5277.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should PR #39 obtain credential-free matrix diagnostics while preserving the complete task, existing repairs, validation gates and authority holds?\\nCandidate-push diagnostics (Recommended): Extend only the ordinary tests workflow to recognize existing agent-visual/<sha> pushes and run opt-in diagnostics on Python 3.11/Textual 0.73 and Python 3.13/Textual 0.89. Disable persisted checkout credentials; retain normal CI unchanged in coverage and strictness. Add ordered test instrumentation, always-retained failure/log/provenance artifacts and complete Ruff output bound to candidate/base/task/run/job/attempt/hashes. Keep protected controller/dispatch/visual workflows unchanged. Require independent plan review before instrumentation, then GitHub evidence and separately reviewed cause-specific repair planning.\"]},{\"choice\":\"pr39_publication_isolation_prerequisite: Separate prerequisite (Recommended)\\nReason: The complete retained user request authorizes reliable repair of the agents' tooling and all task-related blockers, with no heavy checks on the Pi and monitoring through every qualifying successful dev merge. The current reviewed diagnostic plan additionally requires credential-free, disposable unprivileged-container execution while retaining the existing publisher and protected workflows. Immutable pinned-dev source confirms that controller.candidate pushes agent-visual/<commit> and then unconditionally dispatches visual capture. dispatch.py targets agent-visual.yml on main. The observed main commit's controller, dispatch and visual-workflow bytes equal pinned dev; the visual workflow disables persisted checkout credentials but installs candidate code directly on the runner and executes capture beside the trusted exporter. Ordinary tests.yml edits cannot isolate that separate side effect. Commissioning a distinct protected capture-isolation prerequisite therefore resolves a demonstrated operational incompatibility without pretending a publication-only path exists or silently exempting capture from isolation. It keeps PR39 workflow changes confined to ordinary tests.yml and explicitly extends isolation to all candidate execution in newly triggered ordinary CI jobs. Genuine exact-head protected approval, independently reviewed validation and authorized activation must precede using the automatic candidate-publication path. Selecting this prerequisite strategy grants none of those approvals or permissions and requires no new owner fact or repeated preference now.\\n\\nTransparent automated coordinator response after separate independent full-task and immutable-source assessment under the owner's standing recommended-options policy. This selects scope and sequencing only. The coordinator should prepare a concrete, separately reviewed capture-isolation prerequisite through normal signed PR and protected-change processes. Preserve the publisher's exact candidate-SHA/branch/dispatch behavior; do not bypass its automatic capture, invent a publication-only capability, add publishing authority or treat disabled checkout persistence as container isolation. Before any affected temporary candidate publication, verify the prerequisite's actual reviewed head, successful required CI, genuine protected exact-head decision, applicable authorized main/controller synchronization and activation, and exact producer/consumer/runtime evidence under actual freeze/drain holds. This answer is not that decision or deployment permission. Do not repeat completed or cancelled rollouts.\\n\\nKeep PR39 diagnostic workflow edits limited to ordinary tests.yml and retain normal CI coverage, matrix, strict assertions, exit and aggregate failure signals. Any ordinary job newly triggered by candidate pushes that installs, imports, tests, builds or otherwise executes candidate code must use the reviewed isolation boundary too, not only the added diagnostic matrix. Candidate execution must not receive host Git configuration, persisted or write credentials, secrets, privileged controller context or Docker socket; source/output transport and trusted artifact handling remain separate and explicitly reviewed. Preserve current candidate/base/task/plan/checkpoint/patch bindings and Python 3.11/Textual 0.73 plus Python 3.13/Textual 0.89 diagnostic coverage. Require fresh separate whole-plan review before instrumentation.\\n\\nRetain original inputs, assertions, expected values, ordered geometry/readiness/lifecycle observations and actual unresolved right-edge, scroll/resize/narrowing and removal failures. Retain complete setup/call/teardown failure records, tracebacks, stdout/stderr, installed framework source/version provenance and full Ruff output. Always attempt evidence finalization/upload after failure with ordered file lengths/hashes, run/job/attempt identity, missing/unexecuted stages and explicit incompleteness; the retained 100 MiB limit is a collection failure boundary, not permission to truncate silently or turn failed tests green. Fresh GitHub evidence must precede separately reviewed cause-specific behavioral repairs; missing observations remain coordinator-owned, not owner uploads.\\n\\nPreserve all existing and unpublished PR39 SQL Explorer/UI/fixture/completion/journal repairs, incoming current-dev coordinator code/tests/docs and safeguards, warning-only journal failure/recovery, stable parent-relative completion geometry/settled sizing/containment/non-overlap/lifecycle/insert-dismiss behavior, exact picker heading with additive factual correction and no speculative missing-glyph fix, public compatibility, owned changelog/docs, useful regressions and all quality/coverage/debt floors. Retain all 46 scenes at 208x47 cells, every geometry assertion and independent individual full 1280x800 PNG verdict, independent complete-feature/source review and exact-final-head focused/quality/type/coverage/artifact/compatibility/fast CI before correction publication. Diagnostic or prerequisite success alone satisfies none of those feature gates.\\n\\nKeep PR39 as PR37's separate visual-repair dependency, PR37 process-output/history obligations, exporter/producer-consumer/activation gates and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry dependency. Continue monitoring and aligned repairs until every qualifying PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev with required validation, including this prerequisite where relevant. Retain concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, complete questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent full-task resolver and routine-question recovery, one 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance and notification limits. Preserve genuine credentials/authentication/provenance/security, owner veto/cancel, protected exact-head and actual operational holds. No candidate programs, installs, tests or renders run locally or on the Pi. This grants no owner fact, plan/source/visual/CI/protected/deployment approval, hold release, merge clearance or parent-completion claim.\\n\\nExact question and all options:\\n1. How should planning reconcile the existing publisher’s unconditional, non-containerized visual capture with the retained container-isolation requirement and restriction against protected-workflow changes?\\nSeparate prerequisite (Recommended): Have the coordinator commission a separately reviewed protected capture-isolation prerequisite, retaining the existing publisher and dispatch semantics. Keep PR #39 diagnostic workflow changes limited to tests.yml; isolate all candidate execution in newly triggered ordinary CI jobs too. Require genuine exact-head protected approval and authorized activation, respecting freeze/drain holds, before candidate publication. Preserve all repairs, diagnostics, validation and parent obligations; this choice grants no protected approval or deployment permission.\\n\\nIndependent resolution SHA256 c032a36843ae253a527594c6290a6fc2baff87524ab59514b2774313f8d4b8aa.\",\"questions\":[\"1. How should planning reconcile the existing publisher’s unconditional, non-containerized visual capture with the retained container-isolation requirement and restriction against protected-workflow changes?\\nSeparate prerequisite (Recommended): Have the coordinator commission a separately reviewed protected capture-isolation prerequisite, retaining the existing publisher and dispatch semantics. Keep PR #39 diagnostic workflow changes limited to tests.yml; isolate all candidate execution in newly triggered ordinary CI jobs too. Require genuine exact-head protected approval and authorized activation, respecting freeze/drain holds, before candidate publication. Preserve all repairs, diagnostics, validation and parent obligations; this choice grants no protected approval or deployment permission.\"]}],\"images\":[],\"plans\":[{\"approval_index\":null,\"id\":\"57ec0834b8d5c3b3aa194d74b293359d97f120bf37baf5bccc17d0ec0a354d5d\",\"text\":\"# Complete PR #39’s visual repair against current dev\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPreserve PR #39’s existing SQL Explorer repairs and complete two demonstrated corrections: journal failures must show an error without claiming zero matches, and SQL completion menus must leave the active statement readable.\\n\\nPlan against dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`. Assigned GitHub evidence covers published head `a0a9b2fd…`: fast checks passed, visual review rejected it, and complete feature alignment review remains unfinished. Those results do not validate the merged checkout.\\n\\nThe recorded resolver choices settle implementation preferences only; independent plan and implementation reviews remain required.\\n\\n## Implementation and compatibility\\n\\n- **Preserve existing repairs:** retain search highlighting, scrollbar synchronization, create-table controls and validation, type suggestions, help wrapping, consistent visual fixtures, and their regression coverage. Preserve scene IDs and stress scenarios.\\n- **Journal status:** retain the current `journal_screen.py` correction: display `page.warning` alone when present; otherwise display the populated-page status or “No matching journal entries.” Keep `JournalPage` and reader signatures unchanged. Preserve refresh, close, stale-response rejection, and disabled actions after failure.\\n- **Completion placement:** update `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/completion_commands.py` to convert the rendered caret position into the completion menu parent’s coordinates. Include editor content origin, ruler position, gutter, and horizontal/vertical scrolling exactly once. Place the menu’s outer top below the active row.\\n- Prefer below-row placement; use above-row placement when the full menu fits there instead. If neither side fits, constrain height to the larger available space and retain option scrolling. Clamp horizontal placement to available bounds. Never cover the active row; close the menu if no usable space exists.\\n- Reposition after menu layout, candidate narrowing, and visible layout/scroll changes. Ignore deferred work for closed menus or inactive/unmounted workspaces. Preserve completion candidates, insertion ranges, keyboard acceptance, dismissal, and asynchronous stale-result guards.\\n- Strengthen the visual harness with active-row non-overlap and containment assertions for SQL completion scenes. Keep actual application-driven scene configuration.\\n- **Merge conflict:** only the approved coder resolves `docs/CHANGELOG.md`. Remove markers and retain the SQL Explorer repair entry plus all three incoming dev entries. Preserve historical sections and the owned journal fragment; extend that fragment for completion placement without changing package versions.\\n- Update the existing SQL Explorer documentation with completion placement behavior. No public API, storage schema, dependency, or protected workflow change is required.\\n\\n## Focused fast regression coverage\\n\\nRun validation on GitHub, never on the Pi.\\n\\n- Retain journal tests for missing history, successful zero matches, populated results, stale callbacks, corrupt SQLite, unchanged corrupt bytes, disabled actions, and refresh recovery to empty/populated history without executing SQL.\\n- Add completion geometry tests using fake sessions: first-row column completion, later-row CTE/WHERE completion, horizontal and vertical scrolling, tabs/wide characters, resize, right-edge clamping, bottom-edge fallback, and constrained height.\\n- Verify narrowing and asynchronous refresh preserve placement; Enter/Tab insert the selected candidate correctly, Escape dismisses it, and cancelled/deferred callbacks cannot affect another workspace.\\n- Add a negative harness regression proving an intentionally overlapping menu fails the geometry guard.\\n- Retain existing rendered-state and scene-consistency tests. Keep coverage ratchets and quality baselines intact.\\n\\n## GitHub validation and completion\\n\\n1. Obtain fresh independent review of this plan against the pinned base and unresolved changelog conflict before coding.\\n2. Capture the complete SQL Explorer manifest through the established isolated GitHub candidate workflow at **208×47 cells**, producing full **1280×800 PNGs**. Independently inspect every full PNG; require every geometry assertion and individual verdict to pass before correction publication.\\n3. Require final-head focused regressions, quality/coverage/artifact gates, Python compatibility checks, and aggregate `fast-checks`. Obtain complete independent implementation review bound to the final head, dev base, and full task digest. Any subsequent change invalidates affected validation.\\n4. Preserve PR #39 as PR #37’s separate visual-repair dependency. After successful dev merge, the coordinator reconciles and freshly validates PR #37 while preserving its diagnostic/process-output work and historical evidence.\\n5. Continue coordinator-owned monitoring and aligned repairs until every relevant PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev. Preserve separate exporter, producer–consumer, activation, and dependency gates, including PR #10’s actual PR #9 merge/ancestry requirement. Fetch missing evidence through the coordinator.\\n\\n## Retained parent requirements\\n\\nPreserve concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, complete question/answer records, authenticated GitHub and Telegram responses, and resolver alignment review before routine recommendations are selected. Retain the single orchestrator’s 30-minute/open-PR scheduling and idle exit behavior.\\n\\nLimit notifications to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases, and main merges. Relevant `self_host` work concerns GitHub agents only.\\n\\nPreserve credentials, owner veto/cancellation, security/provenance holds, and exact-head protected approvals. Do not repeat completed deployments or treat this repair as proof that the broader operational objective is complete.\\n\"},{\"approval_index\":null,\"id\":\"9dd78fe495470eeefdf8542b35e38997bbb8dea74db104e335bfc6e7a4305123\",\"text\":\"# Complete PR #39’s CI and visual repairs\\n\\n## Summary and evidence\\n\\nPreserve PR #39’s SQL Explorer changes and unpublished repairs. Complete the settled completion-placement, journal-assertion and quality corrections without weakening validation.\\n\\nPlan against dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`. Assigned checks describe published head `6aefc2eff5e37b6d3e98a819ed00b40c9fb244d7`: fast CI failed and independent source review remains unfinished. These results do not validate unpublished edits or a future head.\\n\\nIncorporate factual correction comment `6244524349`: the original picker PNG does not establish character loss. Preserve the original questions, options, answers and resolver receipts; append the correction. The recorded resolver choices settle implementation preferences only. Obtain renewed independent review of this complete replacement plan before coding.\\n\\n## Implementation and compatibility\\n\\n- **Completion placement:** retain and finish the stable parent-relative implementation in `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/completion_commands.py`, with existing style and widget/workspace lifecycle hooks. Use the parent content origin; account for rendered caret cells, ruler, gutter and scrolling once. Set menu dimensions before evaluating settled geometry; never derive the origin from an already-offset menu.\\n- Prefer below-row placement, then above when the full menu fits. Otherwise use the larger available side with constrained height and option scrolling. Clamp horizontally within the parent/editor intersection. Close when the active row is outside the viewport or no usable space remains.\\n- Reposition after opening, narrowing, scrolling and resize. Deferred callbacks must reject closed/replaced menus, stale requests, inactive workspaces, unmounted widgets and modal screens. Repeated placement must converge without drift or refresh loops. Preserve candidates, replacement ranges, Enter/Tab acceptance and Escape dismissal.\\n- **Journal:** retain warning-only failure status in the journal screen and unchanged reader/model signatures. Compare plain displayed text consistently across supported Textual versions in `tests/sql/explorer/journal_screen.py`; preserve exact messages, disabled entry actions, refresh/close availability and recovery behavior.\\n- **Quality and harness:** finish the reported unused-suppression, import-order, complexity, private-access and three completion typing corrections. Keep geometry guards meaningful in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_scene.py`. Preserve coverage floors, debt baselines and all existing assertions.\\n- Retain search highlighting, scrollbar synchronization, create-table controls/validation/type suggestions, help wrapping, coherent fixtures, scene IDs and stress cases. Update the existing SQL Explorer guide and owned changelog fragment; preserve incoming dev and historical changelog entries.\\n- No public API, storage schema, package version, dependency or protected-workflow change is planned. Preserve Python `>=3.8,<3.15` compatibility.\\n\\n## Picker acceptance and explicit exit\\n\\nPreserve the exact heading `Select a .connections database key`, picker interactions and useful text-fidelity coverage. No cause-specific picker or exporter change is justified by the assigned evidence.\\n\\nDuring fresh complete visual review:\\n\\n- If the exact heading and picker scene pass, close the character-loss allegation with the factual correction and fresh evidence. A speculative rendering change or mandatory “missing glyph” repair regression is unnecessary.\\n- If a reviewer identifies a specific unresolved glyph/raster acceptance uncertainty, the coordinator obtains one bounded isolated GitHub diagnostic capture addressing that uncertainty. Bind widget/composed text, raw/framed SVG, raster output and relevant renderer/font provenance to the actual candidate, base, task and run. Historical bytes do not establish current provenance.\\n- If diagnostics demonstrate a defect, obtain cause-specific replanning and independent plan review before repairing the responsible layer. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved; it neither proves character loss nor passes acceptance. Preserve genuine negative controls without presenting synthetic failures as the observed bug.\\n\\n## Focused regression coverage and GitHub validation\\n\\nExecute no programs, tests, installs or rendering locally or on the Pi. Use isolated GitHub validation.\\n\\n- **Completion:** retain focused fake-session tests for first-row columns, multiline CTE/WHERE, tabs/wide characters, both scroll axes, resize, narrowing, right-edge clamping, above-row fallback, constrained-height scrolling and insufficient-space closure. Assert independently calculated settled rectangles, containment and active-row visibility. Verify repeated placement, asynchronous refresh, insertion/dismissal and stale callbacks across tab changes/unmounts.\\n- **Negative geometry control:** first establish a valid popup, then deliberately overlap the active row while retaining containment; require only the visibility guard to fail.\\n- **Journal:** retain missing/empty/populated history, unchanged corrupt bytes, stale responses, disabled actions and recovery to empty/populated results without SQL execution. Require exact displayed text across supported Textual versions.\\n- Retain picker selection/cancellation, exact heading, rendered-state and scene-consistency coverage. Run focused regressions first, followed by required quality, coverage, artifact, supported Python matrix and aggregate `fast-checks`, without relaxing gates.\\n- Through the established isolated candidate workflow, capture all **46 scenes at 208×47 cells**, producing full **1280×800 PNGs**. Require every geometry assertion and independent individual full-PNG verdict to pass before correction publication.\\n- Require fresh complete independent implementation/full-feature alignment review bound to the final head, dev base and complete task digest, plus successful exact-final-head CI. Revalidate affected checks after changes; coordinator refreshes head/dev evidence before publication and merge.\\n\\n## Parent coordination and completion\\n\\n- PR #39 remains PR #37’s separate visual-repair dependency. No catalogue peer merge is required before PR #39 diagnostics or correction publication. After #39 merges into dev, reconcile and freshly validate #37, preserving its diagnostic/process-output and historical-evidence obligations.\\n- Preserve exporter, producer–consumer and activation gates. PR #10 requires PR #9’s actual dev merge and ancestry; that requirement is not a prerequisite for #39.\\n- Continue coordinator-owned monitoring and aligned repairs until **every qualifying PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev**. Verify actual merge state and required ancestry; this leaf repair cannot establish parent completion.\\n- Retain concurrency **10**, truthful lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, complete question/option/answer records, authenticated GitHub and Telegram replies, and independent full-request resolver assessment before selecting routine recommendations. Recover agents waiting on routine questions while preserving genuine owner-input holds.\\n- Retain one global orchestrator, scheduled every 30 minutes while qualifying PRs are open, with idle exit and maintenance across both repositories. Relevant `self_host` work affects GitHub agents only.\\n- Limit notifications to user approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges. Preserve credentials, authentication, provenance/security, owner veto/cancellation and protected exact-head approvals. Preserve operational drain/freeze holds; do not repeat completed deployments or rollouts.\\n\\nThe coordinator supplies missing generated evidence. No owner upload or repeated preference is required, and this plan grants no plan/code/protected approval or deployment authorization.\\n\"},{\"approval_index\":null,\"id\":\"9c666d7aec0665ceb93b0724f277b656c7ded8ef54acf453f16326c840d607f9\",\"text\":\"# Correct PR #39’s changelog fragment and preserve validation gates\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPlan against dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a` and published head `881f73cb5aed4c1d460f1236229a248422d4ae24`.\\n\\nThe owned fragment lacks the `- ` prefix required by the immutable dev-base controller. Correct this verified metadata defect while preserving every existing PR change. The resolver selected this bounded approach; independent plan review remains required.\\n\\nComplete assigned current-head feedback and failed-job logs have now been read. CI remains failed: four completion geometry/lifecycle tests fail across the Python matrix and coverage run. Correcting metadata does not resolve those failures.\\n\\n## Implementation and compatibility\\n\\n- Change only `agent_tools/changelog/04c60facc8294087b55ffdd496a4de82.md` to one UTF-8 line, followed by a final newline:\\n\\n  `- Stabilize SQL completion placement and lifecycle handling, preserve journal failure status, and strengthen geometry regressions.`\\n\\n- Keep the existing fragment identity. Let the established serialized metadata workflow fold it into `docs/CHANGELOG.md`; preserve incoming dev entries, historical sections and unrelated fragments.\\n- Preserve all SQL Explorer changes, unpublished repairs, documentation, regressions, coverage floors and quality baselines.\\n- No public API, model, storage, dependency, package-version or protected-workflow changes are required. Retain Python `>=3.8,<3.15` compatibility.\\n\\n## Focused regression coverage and CI follow-up\\n\\nRun validation exclusively through isolated GitHub mechanisms.\\n\\n- Run existing `tests/repository/changelog_discovery.py` and `tests/repository/changelog_folding.py`. They already cover malformed fragments, correction routing, owner holds, atomic validation, idempotent folding and metadata preservation. No new test is needed for this single-line correction.\\n- Verify the corrected fragment satisfies the existing parser and folds exactly once without changing package or README versions.\\n- Preserve the current CI failures as unresolved evidence: invalid initial geometry in the negative control, failed geometry after scroll/resize/narrowing, right-edge expectation `78 != 79`, and the unmount test’s mounted-state assertion.\\n- Commission cause-specific CI replanning from the complete exact-head logs and matching source, followed by independent plan review before substantive edits. Do not infer causes from assertion output, relax containment/non-overlap checks, remove lifecycle coverage or weaken baselines.\\n\\n## GitHub acceptance\\n\\n- Obtain independent review of this bounded plan before implementation. Refresh head/dev/task bindings before publication; materially changed evidence requires renewed review.\\n- Retain fresh review of all **46 scenes at 208×47 cells**, with full **1280×800 PNGs**, passing geometry assertions and an independent verdict for every image.\\n- Preserve the exact picker heading. Append factual corrections without rewriting question/answer history. Close the character-loss allegation only after fresh acceptance; unresolved uncertainty requires bounded coordinator-owned diagnostics, and a demonstrated defect requires independently reviewed replanning.\\n- Require successful final-head focused regressions, quality, coverage, artifact and supported-Python checks, aggregate `fast-checks`, and complete independent source/full-feature review. Metadata correction alone permits no merge or completion claim.\\n\\n## Parent coordination and retained requirements\\n\\n- Keep PR #39 as PR #37’s separate visual-repair dependency; reconcile and freshly validate #37 after #39 merges. Preserve exporter, producer–consumer and activation gates, and PR #10’s actual PR #9 dev-merge/ancestry requirement.\\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until every qualifying PR and resulting repair merges successfully into dev. Relevant `self_host` PRs affect GitHub agents.\\n- Retain concurrency 10, truthful labels including `agent:writing`, complete questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, independent resolver assessment, and recovery of agents waiting on routine choices.\\n- Retain one global orchestrator scheduled every 30 minutes while qualifying PRs are open, with idle exit. Limit notifications to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges.\\n- Preserve credentials, provenance/security, genuine owner-input, veto/cancel, protected exact-head and operational freeze/drain holds. Do not repeat completed rollouts. No local/Pi execution is authorized.\\n\"},{\"approval_index\":null,\"id\":\"08115be783a40c79468b053769e5bcd569bc2d422d92c03f4a8b20adb794a2a2\",\"text\":\"# Separate protected visual-capture isolation prerequisite\\n\\nPreserve the complete parent task and all original questions/options/answers/plans recorded above. This leaf implements the independently reviewed prerequisite for PR39; it does not complete PR39, PR37, PR9, PR10 or the all-PR monitoring objective.\\n\\nKeep publisher and dispatch semantics, candidate identities, artifact contracts, exact capture step name, 46-scene geometry and every full-PNG review unchanged. Candidate installs/builds/imports/renders execute in two disposable nonroot containers using one resolved official Python image ID and /work/.venv. Installation may reach public Internet through owned firewall guards rejecting private/metadata/host destinations. Rendering has no network. Require read-only root, tmpfs, cap-drop ALL, no-new-privileges, bounded resources and an explicit nonsecret environment. No host secrets, Actions command files, host Git configuration, Docker socket, privileged context or extra mounts enter candidate containers.\\n\\nKeep the Actions checkout pristine; only a private independent copy is writable. Fixed trusted host transports run with Python -I outside candidate ancestry; no host candidate imports/programs or post-execution Git. Require complete owned-container removal before no-follow bounded regular-file collection into fresh host upload destinations. Preserve original artifact bytes, separated failure evidence, exact exits, raw stdout/stderr counts and hashes. Explicitly fail on bounds, unsafe files, incomplete readers or uncertain resource RPCs; retain durable intent and ownership journals and never release guards around surviving/uncertain resources. Setup failures retain honest incomplete envelopes. Quarantine live reader destinations outside uploaded directories.\\n\\nAdd focused adversarial lifecycle/collector/identity/logging/workflow regressions plus docs and a uniquely owned changelog fragment. Do not change SQL Explorer source, visual harness, scene manifest, package versions or public APIs. Add a separately reviewed opt-in native infrastructure probe in tests.yml for Python3.11 and3.13; probe mode skips all ordinary host candidate jobs and executes only fixed reviewed synthetic probe programs inside the same isolation. Prove actual image/Git/venv/native fonts/renderer, public install, host/metadata guard counter hits, private/IPv6 refusal facts and cleanup on GitHub; no-route outcomes are not firewall-hit evidence. Synthetic PNGs grant no visual approval. Local focused and mandatory precommit checks plus fresh complete independent source review, exact-head CI, applicable delegated exact-head protected decision and authorized main activation remain mandatory; no probe/activation approval is inferred from this plan.\\n\\nCommission the real signed prerequisite PR identity first. PR39 retains tests.yml-only diagnostic workflow scope and must independently plan support for representing/verifying all protected approval, activation and operational conditions before affected candidate publication. Preserve real dev-merge/ancestry dependencies, freeze/drain holds, completed/cancelled operation history, concurrency10, truthful labels, full context, authenticated replies, independent resolver/orchestrator policy, notification limits and GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance. Continue monitoring every relevant PR and successor until successful actual dev merges. No candidate tests/builds/scenes run on the Pi.\\n\"}],\"producer_id\":\"local:fc1ed747a0b64317be7ca71679310713\",\"questions\":[{\"answer_index\":18,\"id\":\"bbf852b3d1732f8e55cc51048eb5e9e6cb92346371c93667d256e6c920798d2f\",\"text\":\"1. How should planning proceed while PR #39’s picker character-loss cause remains unproven?\\nDiagnostics first (Recommended): Have the coordinator obtain GitHub glyph/rasterization/scaling diagnostics bound to head 6aefc2eff5e37b6d3e98a819ed00b40c9fb244d7 and dev 7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a, then commission fresh planning and independent plan review. Preserve existing PR changes, unpublished CI repairs, all parent monitoring requirements and authority gates; do not guess a rendering fix or ask the owner to supply evidence.\"}],\"replacements\":[],\"source\":\"user\",\"starting_prompt\":\"implement it on your own if orchestator is not doing that\",\"task_id\":\"fc1ed747a0b64317be7ca71679310713\",\"version\":2}","Agent-authored planning provenance: independently approved bounded atomic lifecycle label implementation. Neither document grants operational approval or changes owner policy; preserve full parent history and separate exact-head requirements.\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"separate-protected-atomic-status-label-replacement-plan\",\n  \"author\": \"/root/review_current_coordinator_routing\",\n  \"status\": \"plan_only_requires_independent_review_before_implementation\",\n  \"objective\": \"Remove the automation-owned DELETE/POST empty-label interval while preserving truthful queued/reviewing/writing and genuine private attention, all unrelated labels, and all existing ownership/gates.\",\n  \"official_api\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://docs.github.com/en/rest/issues/labels#set-labels-for-an-issue\",\n    \"verified\": \"Set labels for an issue: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{issue_number}/labels with labels array replaces the complete existing label set; list endpoint supports per_page up to100 and page. Every PR is an issue. Use PUT, not POST or PATCH.\",\n    \"source_lines\": \"Official docs list labels lines24-49 and set labels lines142-189; read2026-10-19.\"\n  },\n  \"source_bindings\": {\n    \"/Users/karapsin_de/.local/share/analytics-toolkit-agent/sessions/248c02afdc73/19ac2eeff8284a2f/.github/agent/review_control.py\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"1001a4becfef6683f98355299cf797a7d640da9fe12be1f8515dd7b30b4e11d4\",\n      \"bytes\": 52165\n    },\n    \"/Users/karapsin_de/.local/share/analytics-toolkit-agent/sessions/248c02afdc73/19ac2eeff8284a2f/.github/agent/controller.py\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"4ad12163c313fa3d8a05682081954ebc03ddb01052a65765cc908558572f5e4e\",\n      \"bytes\": 57499\n    },\n    \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/self_host/services/github_agent/labels.py\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"150ef33bbd1ded93212ff7bc1a4681d91b63bdcdf496e286f6baf39b1a9bcf77\",\n      \"bytes\": 14870\n    },\n    \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/agent_tools/tests/test_agent_labels.py\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"fc6a55fb64424aae3e2d4fb7219016d46d2edb477d838ec8778e922bc7afa776\",\n      \"bytes\": 16361\n    },\n    \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/agent_tools/tests/test_status_producers.py\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"d384505f021f08528eef1e3703523ee485d45e8526b7f8fac1736c75cefa23e9\",\n      \"bytes\": 16261\n    },\n    \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/agent_tools/tests/test_closed_labels.py\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"2d7f2179e4da8aea4234b0b40b6b1430ba393e8289af580438b178031eb31cae\",\n      \"bytes\": 5674\n    }\n  },\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"primary\": \".github/agent/review_control.py status_transition and narrow safe complete-label read helper, existing trusted producers/callers signature preserved.\",\n    \"tests\": \"Actual controller paired nonintegration tests and existing source-producer contracts; update DELETE/POST assertions to one PUT with complete expected label set.\",\n    \"documentation\": \"Relevant protected controller behavior documentation plus uniquely owned changelog fragment through mandatory version_bump. No unrelated rewrite.\",\n    \"legacy\": \"Existing self_host legacy_transition is intentionally compatibility fallback for older controllers. The protected feature makes every current shared entrypoint use one replacement. Do not silently claim fallback changed; if fallback must change, separate bounded self_host source/compat review/publication is required. No capability downgrade on shared failure.\",\n    \"exclusions\": \"No phase-mapping change, no labels from status paused/capacity, no notification type, no private authority/hold/approval change, no worker/Pi execution or activation implied.\"\n  },\n  \"exact_managed_set\": [\n    \"agent:writing\",\n    \"agent:planning\",\n    \"agent:reviewing\",\n    \"agent:queued\",\n    \"agent:testing\",\n    \"agent:ready\",\n    \"agent:needs-user\"\n  ],\n  \"algorithm\": [\n    \"Under the existing repository/PR reentrant+cross-process status lock, read fresh PR state/head. Fetch complete issue labels explicitly in pages of100. Bound to1000 unique label objects and11 calls including terminal empty/short page; reject malformed/repeated/overflow/failed pagination before any effect. Preserve every name outside the exact seven-name managed set, including other agent-prefixed semantic labels.\",\n    \"Recompute existing private owner_attention and provided pure attention/choose projection on this fresh snapshot. Retain existing expected_state/head rules, owner precedence and remove validation. A known phase yields exactly that phase or needs-user. choose=None preserves unknown existing phase ownership; it is not permission to invent a phase or discard an active writer. Existing closed cleanup removes only requested managed phases and preserves unrelated labels and retained attention.\",\n    \"Immediately before effect, reread fresh state/head and current private attention; rerun choose against current activity and complete latest labels inside the same lock. If labels/head/authority/projection advanced, recompute from fresh inputs, not stale proposed list. Use existing bounded30s/24-iteration convergence budget; deadline checked before each read/mutation. In-flight existing request timeout remains bounded by transport.\",\n    \"If complete desired labels equal latest complete labels, return without any mutation. Otherwise issue ONE PUT issues/N/labels with the complete sorted preserved-nonstatus plus desired-status set. Never DELETE old phase or POST another phase. Validate bounded structured response, then fresh complete-label read and PR/private attention/projection again before success. A single acknowledged PUT is only a single atomic replacement request, not cross-request CAS.\",\n    \"If response is lost or malformed, treat effect as uncertain and read fresh full labels/head/authority before any retry. If the exact current desired set is already present, treat the operation as converged; otherwise recompute and replace under remaining budget. Never blindly POST, blindly restore stale labels, or claim response failure means no effect. Genuine auth/structural/transport errors retain ordinary retry diagnostics; no private state is rewritten.\",\n    \"All cooperating status producers continue sharing the same lock/API. Other publisher/label mutations must be inventoried and routed through this shared path where status ownership is relevant. No global label lock is claimed against independent GitHub actors. Nonstatus additions/removals observed before PUT are preserved; an uncooperative concurrent writer can still cause a lost update between GET and PUT, which must be described honestly. Fresh re-read detects visible drift and normal reconciliation retries.\"\n  ],\n  \"regressions\": [\n    \"Actual paired trusted controller queued\\u2192reviewing, reviewing\\u2192queued, queued\\u2192writing: one PUT and no DELETE/POST/intermediate empty mutation; second identical call performs zero mutations.\",\n    \"Nonstatus labels including semantic agent-prefixed labels on page2+ survive; exact100/1000 boundary and terminal page checked; cap+1/malformed/repeated page/auth failure cause zero writes.\",\n    \"Actual live review Future\\u2192reviewing; done Future/internal wait\\u2192queued; unfinished public agent-review alone does not fake live session. Current source mapping remains unchanged.\",\n    \"Fresh genuine private owner hold wins while Future remains active; derived internal facts/capacity do not invent needs-user; mixed authority remains held.\",\n    \"Owner hold/head/state/Future transition at final preeffect and during PUT, unknown role, closed cleanup/reopen: no old-head decision transfer or authority mutation; fresh retry converges.\",\n    \"Simulate PUT accepted then response lost, PUT not accepted then error, wrong response, external status conflict, concurrent unrelated-label writer. Prove read-before-retry/idempotence, preserve observed nonstatus labels, document unavoidable external-writer race rather than claiming universal atomicity.\",\n    \"Existing writer-lock exact busy retry stays intact; shared errors cannot invoke legacy DELETE/POST fallback; private databases, jobs/Futures, approval and outbox remain unchanged.\"\n  ],\n  \"workflow\": \"Root owns NEW managed task/feature branch off actual current dev after mandatory startup/revalidation; never modify handed-off PR47 or another author branch. Full task context and this plan retained. After independent plan approval, implement, focused meaningful regressions, complete fresh source/compat review and mandatory full precommit/CI. Protected exact-head approval is a distinct later authorized decision; main projection/activation also requires separate exact reviewed compatibility sequencing. No approval is granted by this plan.\",\n  \"limits\": \"No live GitHub label or Pi mutation performed. A one-PUT replacement eliminates our internal remove/add window; GitHub provides no per-label-set CAS and this plan cannot guarantee permanent uniqueness or no lost unrelated-label update against noncooperating external writers.\"\n}\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"independent-complete-protected-label-plan-review\",\n  \"reviewer\": \"/root/resolve_pr29_compact_test_question\",\n  \"author\": \"/root/review_current_coordinator_routing\",\n  \"decision\": \"approve_plan\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"subject\": {\n    \"path\": \"/private/tmp/protected-atomic-status-label-replacement-concrete-plan-v1.json\",\n    \"bytes\": 8732,\n    \"sha256\": \"85df619a687fa9d7f4d9105b691148728f493bb782e77e4523b68963399da033\"\n  },\n  \"scope\": \"Whole8732-byte protected-controller atomic managed-status replacement PLAN, grounded in actual cited controller/shared-status/worker/legacy/tests interfaces. Exact new source/task/enrollment/CI/policy/admission/main/activation are separate later gates.\",\n  \"context_and_method\": {\n    \"full_user_task_sha256\": \"9e234588b44a3310e115541df26b8c2765e20dc40c4a8224cb471d4f3756ed14\",\n    \"starting_prompt\": \"implement it on your own if orchestator is not doing that\",\n    \"repository_startup\": \"Mandatory repository MCP prepare_start completed with clean dev/reused environment/no blockers; RAG docs query then routed agent_tools/README and relevant operations lifecycle contract read. No feature/Git/source edit, check/test/import or label mutation performed.\",\n    \"read_scope\": \"Complete frozen plan, six cited exact source bindings, actual status_lock/status_transition/_preserve_phase/owner_attention/reconcile_label, GitHub.api/pages/pull/label, complete worker labels.py and narrow actual paired/legacy test producer interfaces. Searched all current protected/worker label mutation callsites. Official REST documentation independently opened read-only.\",\n    \"source_bindings\": {\n      \"/Users/karapsin_de/.local/share/analytics-toolkit-agent/sessions/248c02afdc73/19ac2eeff8284a2f/.github/agent/review_control.py\": {\n        \"bytes\": 52165,\n        \"sha256\": \"1001a4becfef6683f98355299cf797a7d640da9fe12be1f8515dd7b30b4e11d4\",\n        \"matches_plan\": true\n      },\n      \"/Users/karapsin_de/.local/share/analytics-toolkit-agent/sessions/248c02afdc73/19ac2eeff8284a2f/.github/agent/controller.py\": {\n        \"bytes\": 57499,\n        \"sha256\": \"4ad12163c313fa3d8a05682081954ebc03ddb01052a65765cc908558572f5e4e\",\n        \"matches_plan\": true\n      },\n      \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/self_host/services/github_agent/labels.py\": {\n        \"bytes\": 14870,\n        \"sha256\": \"150ef33bbd1ded93212ff7bc1a4681d91b63bdcdf496e286f6baf39b1a9bcf77\",\n        \"matches_plan\": true\n      },\n      \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/agent_tools/tests/test_agent_labels.py\": {\n        \"bytes\": 16361,\n        \"sha256\": \"fc6a55fb64424aae3e2d4fb7219016d46d2edb477d838ec8778e922bc7afa776\",\n        \"matches_plan\": true\n      },\n      \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/agent_tools/tests/test_status_producers.py\": {\n        \"bytes\": 16261,\n        \"sha256\": \"d384505f021f08528eef1e3703523ee485d45e8526b7f8fac1736c75cefa23e9\",\n        \"matches_plan\": true\n      },\n      \"/private/tmp/atk-controller-admission-self-host/agent_tools/tests/test_closed_labels.py\": {\n        \"bytes\": 5674,\n        \"sha256\": \"2d7f2179e4da8aea4234b0b40b6b1430ba393e8289af580438b178031eb31cae\",\n        \"matches_plan\": true\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"official_contract\": {\n    \"url\": \"https://docs.github.com/en/rest/issues/labels#set-labels-for-an-issue\",\n    \"support\": \"Official Set labels endpoint uses PUT and full labels array replaces existing labels. List labels supports per_page up to100 and explicit page; pull requests share issue label endpoints. This supports a single replacement mutation rather than a remove/add pair; it does not establish a per-label-set CAS or an atomic transaction with local authority.\",\n    \"docs_sections\": \"List labels lines24-49; Set labels lines142-189 at independent read.\",\n    \"no_verbatim_large_quote\": true\n  },\n  \"actual_interfaces\": {\n    \"protected_boundary\": \"review_control.py59-127 exposes status_transition(gh,number,head,choose,attention=None,remove=frozenset(),expected_state=open). Exact managed universe is6PHASES plus PAUSED. snapshot rechecks exact PR state/head and private owner_attention, but reads only default first label page. Current conflict branch DELETEs one phase before POSTing the missing phase, making an automation-created zero-phase interval real.\",\n    \"mutex\": \"review_control.py26-56 actual per-state/repository/number RLock and thread nesting; when AGENT_STATE_DIR configured on POSIX, shared path status-locks/sha(repo:number).lock and nonblocking FLOCK adds host cross-process serialization. Without that environment only in-process locking is available; no GitHub-global or external actor exclusion. Keep exact exception/origin behavior because worker acquire_writer recognizes the real lock TimeoutError.\",\n    \"adapter\": \"controller.py149-154 GitHub.api already accepts arbitrary method and structured data and passes JSON through gh api --method/--input. No new endpoint, RPC or private worker API is required for PUT labels or explicit numbered GET pages. GitHub.pages156-159 is unbounded generic paginate; the new bounded labels helper should use explicit api pages rather than claim generic pages enforces the1000/11 budget. Existing command transport has a180s in-flight timeout;30s transition deadline bounds additional calls/checks, not a hard total wall guarantee.\",\n    \"owner_precedence\": \"owner_attention572-593 reads current private veto/pause/attention hint and conservatively surfaces unknown security reasons. status display does not call authenticated recovery to create authority. Existing connect/schema machinery is retained; proposed status change must not add authority/job/outbox mutations. expectedclosed preserves retained needs-user while cleaning eligible phases.\",\n    \"actual_current_writers\": \"GitHub.label176-182 calls shared status_transition for acquire/release. _attention_display and reconcile_label also call it. Worker labels.transition/acquire_writer/reconcile/reconcile_closed select the trusted shared function when available. daemon/intake/controller release sites use gh.label, so they enter the same protected boundary. Search found no other protected direct label DELETE/POST writers outside review_control; worker legacy_transition and legacy closed cleanup are distinct explicitly retained compatibility paths.\",\n    \"activity_projection_limit\": \"Worker live_phase reads actual active Futures at each callback invocation and distinguishes readonly planning/reviewing from writing. labels.reconcile does capture pending=requests(...) before shared transition, and desired callback closes over that snapshot. Constant writer-acquisition callbacks and _preserve_phase do not expose an independent fresh full task/request ownership provider. Re-running the supplied choose refreshes only the actual data its existing callback reads. Do not describe unchanged API as fetching a fresh full task/request/DB ownership snapshot or universal activity CAS; durable request changes can require normal next reconciliation. This does not block the narrow display mutation repair or justify inventing a remote endpoint/callback.\",\n    \"none_and_terminal\": \"choose=None means unknown existing phase ownership, not remove-all. Writer release removes only requested writing through remove while preserving another phase; genuine attention can suppress phases without releasing Future. Explicit terminal closed/no-live projection may clear only permitted managed phases, preserving unrelated labels and retained attention. Do not reinterpret None as blanket cleanup.\"\n  },\n  \"whole_plan_assessment\": {\n    \"minimal_cause_fix\": \"One complete PUT removes our own two-request remove/add interval without changing queued/reviewing/writing source mapping, worker concurrency or authority. Full unrelated names are part of every desired set; only the exact seven managed names are controller-owned. Other agent-prefixed labels are semantic labels and remain untouched.\",\n    \"complete_read_and_bounds\": \"Fetch actual complete labels by numbered100-page requests with1000 unique-label/11-call terminal bounds. Check deadline before every page/read/mutation. Malformed objects/names, repeated identities/pages, unknown result shape, failed pagination and overflow must refuse before PUT, not truncate. Exactly1000 must verify terminal page; cap+1 refuses. A latest complete read is necessary immediately before replacement, not a first-page union with stale pull labels.\",\n    \"projection_and_preeffect\": \"Within same actual status lock, retain expectedhead/state, owner precedence, remove validation and known/unknown ownership semantics. Recheck real current owner attention and fresh head/state/latest complete labels, and rerun existing choose/attention callbacks. Drift recomputes within bounded convergence; head change aborts old decision rather than transferring it. No task or owner fact is inferred from public labels.\",\n    \"single_effect\": \"If full desired set equals latest full set, no write. Else PUT the complete sorted preserved nonmanaged+correct managed set once per convergence attempt. Do not DELETE/POST a phase or fallback on shared failure. Validate returned shape within bounds, then actual fresh complete labels/head/current attention/projection before declaring convergence.\",\n    \"uncertain_effect\": \"Lost/malformed/error PUT is an uncertain effect, not proof of no write. Perform fresh bounded GET/head/authority read before considering another mutation; if latest desired actualset present, converge without anotherPUT, otherwise recompute. No blind stale restore/add/remove retry. Persistent auth/structural errors remain ordinary retry failures, no blanket ignore/private-state rewrite.\",\n    \"honest_races\": \"Single replacement request is narrower than cross-request/private-system CAS. A noncooperating actor may add/remove an unrelated label after finalGET and beforePUT, or server-visible completion may lag. Current observed unrelated labels are preserved; permanent no-lost-update against such actors is not proven. Fresh observed drift and periodic reconciler remain recovery, never reported as universal prevention.\",\n    \"legacy_scope\": \"Old controllers lacking the shared capability continue current self_host legacy paths, including DELETE/POST. This feature cannot claim their behavior fixed or no-empty-interval globally before real protected controller publication/admission/activation. Shared capability execution failure must propagate without legacy downgrade. Any fallback rewrite needs separate bounded self_host source/compat/publication scope.\",\n    \"no_new_noise_or_attention\": \"No worker-paused/capacity→needs-user mapping, new TG event, source of approval or owner-question recovery is introduced. Full user notification limits, truthful active ownership and genuine owner/security/provenance/veto/cancel holds remain. Closed/open transitions do not grant merge or release private Future.\",\n    \"workflow_boundary\": \"New owned ATK task/feature only through mandatory startup/revalidation; preserve handed-off47 and independent RouteB author branches. Retain full user task and exact plan, relevant documentation and owned fragment. Fresh independent cumulative source/compatibility review, meaningful focused/fullprecommit/CI and applicable protected exact-head decision/current controller admission/main origin/activation are separate. Existing frozen controller chains and completed operations cannot be retargeted.\"\n  },\n  \"source_grounded_test_constraints\": [\n    \"Use a new exact candidate-bound paired controller fixture or actual new-controller unit source for newPUT assertions. The current self_host test_status_producers EXPECTED fixture pins b00035/b5f803 with base98e4236, not the current b59/root1001/4ad bytes nor future newfeature; those historical tests alone do not validate newsource. Preserve its historical identity/receipt or add an explicitly versioned successor fixture.\",\n    \"Current test_agent_labels tests with controller=None deliberately exercise unchanged legacy DELETE/POST, e.g writer acquisition300-308; do not blindly replace those expectations withPUT. Add new shared-controller tests for new behavior while keeping meaningful legacy compatibility tests.\",\n    \"Teach fake issue endpoint real explicit pagination and PUT full-replacement semantics, successful structured response and post-call snapshots. A fake that ignores methodPUT or returns its whole set for every page cannot prove no empty window/paging/preservation.\",\n    \"Verify queued↔reviewing and writer acquisition each use onePUT/noDELETEorPOST/neverempty intermediate mutation, then identical reconciliation zero writes. Include unrelated semantic agent labels and page2 names.\",\n    \"Test exact100/1000/terminal page,1001/malformed/repeated/overflow/auth failure with zero mutations; full current unrelatedlabel preservation.\",\n    \"Actual Future active/done/internal wait and unknown live role, genuine owner hold precedence, final preeffect/duringPUT head/state/hold/Future drift, release remove-only-writing and close/reopen retain private ownership; no fake public review equals live session.\",\n    \"PUT accepted+response loss, not accepted+error, malformed response, external controlled conflict and unrelated label writer each require read-before-retry/honest convergence; preserve immutable privateDB/jobs/Futures/outbox/approvals. Existing exact busy-origin retry and no legacy fallback on sharederrors remain.\",\n    \"Document API/external/private CAS limitations and pending historical fallback behavior; no test assertion pretends a truly concurrent external lost-update is prevented.\"\n  ],\n  \"remaining_precision_not_new_scope\": \"The approved contract is freshness of actual head/state/complete labels/private attention plus actual supplied callback observations, not an invented global fresh-task provider. If implementation chooses to require stronger fresh full request/private activity before PUT, first provide the genuine caller-bound datasource and separately assess that narrow API/callsite change. It is unnecessary to invent it for this request-window fix.\",\n  \"full_user_objective_retained\": \"Continue aligned repairs and all qualifying PR/successor actual successful dev merges; retain full features/all46 visual gates, source/CI/auth/provenance/dependency/runtime/main/protected holds, concurrency10, complete authenticatedQ/options/A, independent recommended resolver, singleton30min/relevant-open-PR orchestrator, no-heavy-Pi and notification restrictions. This label plan is a leaf design, not full-parent completion.\",\n  \"limits\": {\n    \"plan_approved_for_exact_subject_only\": true,\n    \"source_approved\": false,\n    \"tests_or_candidate_programs_run\": false,\n    \"GitHub_label_or_Pi_mutation\": false,\n    \"API_calls_to_user_repository\": false,\n    \"official_docs_read_only\": true,\n    \"newowner_or_protected_approval\": false,\n    \"controller_admission_main_or_runtime_activation\": false,\n    \"global_atomicity_or_external_race_immunity\": false,\n    \"all_PR_completion\": false\n  },\n  \"next_step\": \"Implement the exact narrow protected-controller replacement in a new owned feature after normal managed workflow; retain these actual-interface/test constraints and obtain fresh complete source/compatibility and required validation. Do not mutate live labels or deploy from this plan verdict.\"\n}\n","AGENT-AUTHORED IMPLEMENTATION AND VALIDATION PROVENANCE. This is an agent-generated factual record, not a new human request, answer, decision, protected policy approval or operational authorization. The exact starting user prompt and every prior full parent/task/plan/correction are retained unchanged.\n\nThe reviewed atomic PR status-label feature uses one complete-set GitHub PUT while preserving all unrelated labels, checks the exact seven managed status labels, bounds paged reads and projected writes, and retains fresh head/phase/attention checks around the operation. No broad external-writer atomicity or private authority mutation is claimed. Ten current ATK source/context members remain byte-identical to the complete V3 inventory; only the explicit nine changed feature paths are to be published. Source review, actual full local checks, CI/review, exact-head owner policy authority, dev merge, main projection and runtime activation are separate facts. Local success grants none of the latter. Paired self_host producer fixtures were separately tested with explicitly simulated authority and remain unpublished source there.\n\nThe complete independent V3 source review and complete actual mandatory validation assessment follow as agent provenance. Original failing attempts, root-cause corrections and raw logs remain preserved. All four mandatory stages and all nine matrix profiles actually executed successfully on the exact unchanged source; no stale-stage substitution or validation weakening. Existing setuptools artifact-build deprecations are recorded honestly as a separate deferred follow-up; pytest runs had no warning summary.\n\nWhole independent source review original:\n{\n  \"schema\": \"independent-whole-atomic-status-controller-source-task-plan-review-v3\",\n  \"author\": \"/root\",\n  \"reviewer\": \"/root/review_separate_visual_repair_final_source\",\n  \"decision\": \"APPROVE_SOURCE\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"source_only\": true,\n  \"scope\": \"Fresh whole cumulative source/task/plan review of the exact current declared atomic-status unit, with complete reread of3changed test/helper bodies. Source-only, no validation or operational approval.\",\n  \"subject\": {\n    \"inventory\": \"/private/tmp/atomic-status-controller-complete-source-inventory-v3.json\",\n    \"inventory_sha256\": \"e16891a70aa9a5fbd2cf7b9b056d1fbc8da1b081d95def0809e10169eb4cfbe7\",\n    \"snapshot\": \"/private/tmp/atomic-status-controller-complete-source-freeze-v3\",\n    \"members\": 29,\n    \"all29_complete_file_hashes_and_lengths_verified\": true,\n    \"base\": \"f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01\",\n    \"branch\": \"codex/19ac2eeff8284a2f-92b2a202\",\n    \"task_id\": \"12c7a273d1c84f48bcb6abfb9e3c6caa\",\n    \"task_digest\": \"90092c5ae7552a65d2ff2c61d89566a22d0bc09d37a8a10d82e76523344c4375\"\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/.github/agent/controller.py\",\n      \"bytes\": 57499,\n      \"sha256\": \"4ad12163c313fa3d8a05682081954ebc03ddb01052a65765cc908558572f5e4e\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/.github/agent/review_control.py\",\n      \"bytes\": 53844,\n      \"sha256\": \"5b75b431f9768617e9bb75b6c9689a961a9bec4aa568a58ed0a9749af37143a6\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/agent_tools/changelog/7211c07be7c7433c910e331e45fff12e.md\",\n      \"bytes\": 115,\n      \"sha256\": \"57dfdadec5386282e549e77304825a4f675e984642dc093edf309c49abbb58f4\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/docs/GITHUB_AGENT_OPERATIONS.md\",\n      \"bytes\": 61769,\n      \"sha256\": \"69006c9a27041894c0895d5c155cc4ac909206bc358ad21e30eafd2ee1ff4061\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/tests/repository/_support/label_api.py\",\n      \"bytes\": 2835,\n      \"sha256\": \"8c7395f1a1934c5952d3151e5e78468c70997e2679e6f17ebcd1905cba853314\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/tests/repository/_support/publication.py\",\n      \"bytes\": 6185,\n      \"sha256\": \"5ba263c83cf71a59ca81dd6fe350cb2c268cda25592b607edb290f1184680e34\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/tests/repository/atomic_status.py\",\n      \"bytes\": 6589,\n      \"sha256\": \"3a6fc343c2890b11abfbd770b6a1ffb735d1808c43c3ffde9b21ba991ea48cd4\",\n      \"verified\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"atk/tests/repository/github_agent.py\",\n      \"bytes\": 23786,\n      \"sha256\": \"0730127ec4be14bcb7764f8abebdbbedc21ab302